// Condensed matter layer: powders, liquids and placeable solids (tile 8, element id in the material byte).
// Appended after sim.wgsl. Matter cells are solid obstacles for the gas solver; they carry a temperature,
// a state flag, an emission code and a remaining fraction in WALL = (T, flag, code, remaining).
//
// Element ids (walls are 0-9; matter 10..N_ELEM-1). elements.rs MATTER_INFO mirrors these tables.
// 10 sand, 11 charcoal, 12 sulfur, 13 saltpeter KNO3, 14 sugar, 15 aluminium powder, 16 ammonium perchlorate,
// 17 rust (iron oxide), 18 ammonium nitrate, 19 water, 20 kerosene, 21 ethanol, 22 liquid oxygen,
// 23 nitroglycerin, 24 molten metal, 25 ash/slag,
// 26 ice, 27 snow, 28 salt, 29 brine, 30 liquid nitrogen, 31 gasoline, 32 diesel, 33 cooking oil, 34 napalm,
// 35 wax, 36 molten wax, 37 coal, 38 paper, 39 magnesium, 40 iron filings, 41 sodium, 42 potassium,
// 43 lye (NaOH solution), 44 hydrochloric acid, 45 hydrogen peroxide (HTP), 46 manganese dioxide,
// 47 potassium perchlorate, 48 nitrocellulose, 49 TNT, 50 C4, 51 dynamite, 52 blasting cap, 53 glass,
// 54 molten glass, 55 lava, 56 stone, 57 gunpowder, 58 dry ice, 59 copper oxide, 60 potassium permanganate,
// 61 glycerin, 62 plastic, 63 molten plastic, 64 flour, 65 fuse,
// 66 HTPB binder, 67 epoxy binder, 68 copper chromite (catalyst), 69 potassium chlorate, 70 sodium nitrate,
// 71 titanium powder, 72 zinc powder, 73 red phosphorus, 74 sorbitol, 75 dextrose, 76 rubber, 77 cotton,
// 78 coal dust, 79 sawdust, 80 acetone, 81 methanol, 82 nitric acid, 83 hydrazine, 84 N2O4, 85 tungsten,
// 86 graphite, 87 phenolic ablative, 88 phenolic char, 89 fibreglass, 90 firebrick, 91 aerogel
//
// CAST / PRESSED grains: META dir byte bit 0 (bit 16 of META) on a tile-8 cell = packed solid (immobile, porous no
// more). Packed oxidiser/fuel mixtures react ONLY at gas-exposed surface cells, r = a p^n (see cast_burn); loose
// powder keeps the fast bulk deflagration. Op kind 9 (sim.wgsl apply_ops) sets the bit; over-pressure clears it
// (WALL.y request 0.94 -> apply_conversion) = cracked grain = CATO.
//
// Gas mapping (the gas state has 4 species + soot): fuel slot x = CH4-like fuel AND hydrogen, fuel vapours,
// pyrolysis gas; y = O2 (LOX boil-off, oxidiser decomposition, peroxide); z = inert N2-like (LN2 boil-off);
// w = products CO2 / H2O (steam, dry-ice CO2, HCl fumes, reaction products); soot = smoke.
//
// WALL.y for matter cells (commit in sim.wgsl acts only on >= 1):
//   0.0 fresh (just placed: the first update applies E_TINIT), 0.1..0.5 settled with phase-change progress
//   p = (y - 0.1) / 0.4, 0.55 + id/1000 = request: turn into element id (done by the movement pass),
//   1.5 consumed -> gas, 1.6 burst into hot gas, 1.7 molten iron, 1.8 slag, 2.0 detonation, 3.0 molten metal freezes.

